course: dictionary
lesson: 733
title: Basically
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Basically» means in the most important way, or the main idea when you think about it. It can also sum something up simply. «Basically, we lost.» The speaker is giving the main point, not every detail of the game.
explain: People often say «basically» in speech, as a filler to sum things up. «We're both adopted, so we're basically twins,» she jokes. She means they are alike in the main way, even though they are not really twins.
explain: In your own school writing, «basically» can give the main idea, but formal writing often prefers «in short» or «mainly». Ask yourself: is this the main point, or am I just filling a gap with a word?
fact: Basically means in the most important way, or simply put.
fact: «Basically» is an adverb: it tells you more about how something is true or done.
fact: Words ending in -ic add -ally: basic, basically; dramatic, dramatically.
fact: The famous exception is «publicly», not «publically».
fact: «The Sun's light is basically white» means its main colour is white. Our air scatters blue light, so the Sun looks yellowish, and from space it looks white.
exercise: «Basically, we lost.» What does basically tell the reader? | The time of the match | *The main point, said simply | A question about the game | A long list of every detail
exercise: Which is the correct adverb from «basic»? | basicaly | *basically | basicly | basicallly
exercise: Mia says, «We're basically twins.» What does she mean? | They are sisters who never argue | They were born on the same day | They are exactly the same height and age | *They are alike in the main way, though not really twins
test: What does basically show in «The Sun's light is basically white»? | *The main idea: its light is mostly white | The Sun is always yellow | The light is cold | The light is blue at night
test: Which word is the exception to the -ic and -ally rule? | dramatically | *publicly | publically | basically
exam: Which sentence uses basically to sum up simply? | «The sky turned red, dramatically.» | «He ran basically.» | «The basic shape is a square.» | *«Basically, the match was lost by one goal.»
